        "populationConfidence": "approximate",
        "ruler": "Romulus, by tradition",
        "story": "The traditional founding date. What stands on the Palatine is a cluster of huts inside a ditch and a timber fence — one of several villages scattered across the hills above a ford on the Tiber. Livy, writing seven centuries later, tells the story of Romulus and Remus and admits at the outset that the accounts are poetic rather than historical.",
        "seeing": "huts on the Palatine behind a timber palisade, the other hills still empty, and the Tiber running below the ford. Nothing here is monumental yet.",
        "sourceIds": ["livy-1-6-7"],
        "unsourcedClaims": ["the size of the settlement"]
