      "name": "the city of the popes",
      "dossier": {
        "population": null,
        "populationLabel": "a few tens of thousands",
        "populationConfidence": "approximate",
        "ruler": "Pope Leo III",
        "story": "On Christmas Day, Leo III crowns Charlemagne emperor in Old St Peter's. The city that watches is a fraction of the one that built the Colosseum: the Aurelian Walls, thrown up in haste five centuries earlier, now enclose more ruins and gardens than houses, and the living city has drifted into the river bend for its water. Einhard, who knew Charlemagne, claims he would not have entered the church that day had he known what the pope intended. The papal account tells it differently.",
        "seeing": "the Aurelian circuit far out around a city that no longer fills it, Old St Peter's across the Tiber, and the Colosseum and Pantheon still standing among the gardens.",
